## Mission

- Help visitors understand the furniture service quickly.
- Reduce the burden of comparing prices and visiting stores.
- Build trust with clear value, responsive content, and authentic testimonials.
- Guide visitors to apply, inquire, sign up, or start the service through a clear CTA.
- Treat `docs/PRD.md` as the single source of truth.
- Read `.cubivora/TEAM.md` and `.cubivora/Memory.md` before planning or coding.
- Update `docs/PRD.md` in the same commit when implementation decisions diverge from it.

## North-star metric

- Maximize the CTA click conversion rate.
- Calculate it as unique CTA clickers divided by unique landing-page visitors.
- Measure landing-page visits and CTA clicks consistently across mobile and desktop.
<!-- TBD: No baseline or target CTA conversion rate is provided. -->

## Killer differentiator

- Let furniture shoppers compare options without the inconvenience of visiting multiple stores.
- Connect credible customer outcomes directly to the visitor’s price-comparison and store-visit concerns.
- Keep the path from discovery to application or inquiry fast and consistent on every supported device.

## Primary personas

- Furniture shoppers planning an upcoming purchase.
- Price-conscious customers comparing furniture options.
- Customers who find in-person store visits inconvenient.

## Top user journeys

- Discover the page through search and understand the service from its title, description, and primary content.
- Recognize the brand from the persistent, undistorted logo.
- Review the service value and furniture price-comparison benefits.
- Read authentic testimonials about easier comparisons or fewer store visits.
- Select the primary CTA on mobile or desktop.
- Continue to the designated sign-up, application, inquiry, or service-start page without errors.
- Record the landing-page visit and CTA click for conversion analysis.
- Select the logo to return to the landing-page start or the main service page.